    {
      "page_title": "Why Multi-Stage",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. What is it?",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A ==multi-stage== Dockerfile has several `FROM` lines",
            "Each `FROM` starts a new stage with a **fresh** filesystem",
            "Only the last stage (or the `--target` stage) is the final image",
            "Earlier stages are discarded from the shipped image"
          ],
          "style": "star",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Example",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "dockerfile",
          "lines": [
            "FROM golang:1.22 AS build",
            "RUN go build -o /app ./cmd/server",
            "",
            "FROM alpine",
            "COPY --from=build /app /app"
          ],
          "note": "Only the alpine stage ships"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Read it as",
          "text": "Stage 1 compiles the binary. Stage 2 copies only /app out of it."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Before vs after",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "",
            "Single-stage",
            "Multi-stage"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Base",
              "golang:1.22",
              "alpine"
            ],
            [
              "Size",
              "~800 MB",
              "small runtime"
            ],
            [
              "Contains",
              "toolchain, source, module cache",
              "binary only"
            ],
            [
              "Files",
              "1 Dockerfile",
              "1 Dockerfile"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Old way: the ==builder pattern==, two Dockerfiles",
            "A shell script copied artifacts out via `docker cp`",
            "Multi-stage: one Dockerfile, one `docker build`"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Faster pull and faster deploy",
            "Lower registry cost",
            "Smaller **attack surface**"
          ],
          "style": "checkbox",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Measure the win",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "docker build -t app:fat .",
            "docker images app",
            "# REPOSITORY  TAG  SIZE",
            "# app         fat  ~800MB"
          ],
          "note": "compare before and after"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Same app, same code, only the **final stage** changes",
            "Typical Go service drops from ~800 MB to ~10 MB",
            "Smaller images pull faster in CI and on cold nodes"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Inspect layers",
          "text": "`docker history app:fat` shows which layer holds the toolchain bulk."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Common mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Leaving `gcc`, `git`, npm devDependencies in the final stage",
            "Assuming earlier stages get pushed: they stay only in the local build cache",
            "Forgetting intermediate stages still cost build time and cache space"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Key rule",
          "text": "Build in one stage, ship from another. Next: naming stages and COPY --from."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "docker",
      "subtitle": "The single-stage problem"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Naming Stages and COPY --from",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. What is a stage name?",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`FROM image AS name` gives a ==stage== a name",
            "Without `AS`, stages are numbered from **0**",
            "Names are case-insensitive, lowercase by convention",
            "Usual names: `build`, `deps`, `test`, `runtime`"
          ],
          "style": "star",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "dockerfile",
          "lines": [
            "# stage 0, named build",
            "FROM node:20 AS build",
            "FROM node:20-slim AS runtime",
            "# stage 2, unnamed",
            "FROM alpine"
          ],
          "note": "unnamed stages only get an index"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. How COPY --from works",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              {
                "text": "build stage",
                "sub": "/src/out",
                "ink": "blue"
              },
              {
                "text": "COPY --from",
                "sub": "files only",
                "ink": "purple"
              },
              {
                "text": "runtime stage",
                "sub": "/app",
                "ink": "green"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Source",
            "Syntax"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Named stage",
              "`--from=build`"
            ],
            [
              "Stage index",
              "`--from=0`"
            ],
            [
              "External image",
              "`--from=nginx:1.27`"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "dockerfile",
          "lines": [
            "COPY --from=build /src/out /app",
            "COPY --from=nginx:1.27 \\",
            "  /etc/nginx/nginx.conf /tmp/"
          ],
          "note": "prefer names; index breaks on reorder"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Only files travel",
          "text": "==ENV==, WORKDIR, USER and installed packages do **not** carry over from the source stage."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Example and options",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "dockerfile",
          "lines": [
            "FROM node:20 AS build",
            "RUN npm ci && npm run build",
            "FROM node:20-slim AS runtime",
            "COPY --from=build /app/dist /app/dist",
            "COPY --from=build /app/node_modules \\",
            "  /app/node_modules"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`FROM base AS dev` reuses base layers and ENV",
            "`--chown=app:app` sets ownership during the copy",
            "`--link` (BuildKit) makes the layer independent",
            "With `--link`, base changes do not invalidate it"
          ],
          "style": "dot"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Reading the errors",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Error",
            "Likely cause"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`invalid from flag value`",
              "stage name not defined"
            ],
            [
              "`pull access denied`",
              "name treated as image"
            ],
            [
              "`not found` on COPY",
              "wrong path in source stage"
            ],
            [
              "wrong files copied",
              "index shifted by reorder"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "dockerfile",
          "lines": [
            "COPY --link --chown=app:app \\",
            "  --from=build /app/dist /app/dist"
          ],
          "note": "combine both flags in one COPY"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Copy the **narrowest** path you need",
            "Check the source stage with `--target build`",
            "Name stages so reorders stay safe"
          ],
          "style": "checkbox",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Peek inside a stage",
          "text": "`docker build --target build -t dbg .` then `docker run --rm dbg ls /app` shows what a COPY can reach."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Rule",
          "text": "Name every stage, copy narrow paths, and use `--chown` plus `--link`."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Checklist",
          "text": "Named stage, narrow path, one `COPY --from` per artifact. Next page: build cache."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "docker",
      "subtitle": "Naming stages"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "COPY --from Mistakes and Stage Inheritance",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Common mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Unknown stage gives `invalid from flag value`",
            "Or `pull access denied`: treated as an image name",
            "`COPY --from=0` after reordering stages grabs the wrong one",
            "COPY copies the **whole path**, build artifacts included"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Fixing each mistake",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Mistake",
            "Fix"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Unknown stage name",
              "add `AS name` to FROM"
            ],
            [
              "`--from=0` after reorder",
              "use `--from=build`"
            ],
            [
              "Whole path copied",
              "copy `/app/dist` only"
            ],
            [
              "Typo in stage name",
              "match `AS` exactly"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "dockerfile",
          "lines": [
            "# risky: index shifts on reorder",
            "COPY --from=0 /app /app",
            "# safe: the name never changes",
            "COPY --from=build /app/dist /app"
          ],
          "note": "names survive stage reordering"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Copy only what ships",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`COPY --from=build /app /app` also copies sources and caches",
            "Narrow it: `/app/dist` holds the compiled output",
            "Add `node_modules` only if the runtime needs it",
            "Run `ls` in the build stage to confirm paths"
          ],
          "style": "star",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "dockerfile",
          "lines": [
            "FROM node:20 AS build",
            "RUN npm ci && npm run build",
            "FROM node:20-slim AS runtime",
            "COPY --from=build /app/dist /app"
          ],
          "note": "runtime gets output, not sources"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Building on a stage",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A stage can start `FROM` an earlier stage",
            "`FROM base AS dev` reuses its layers and ==ENV==",
            "Plain `COPY --from` brings files only, not ENV",
            "Shared setup lives once in a `base` stage"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "dockerfile",
          "lines": [
            "FROM node:20-slim AS base",
            "ENV NODE_ENV=production",
            "WORKDIR /app",
            "FROM base AS runtime",
            "COPY --from=build /app/dist ."
          ],
          "note": "runtime inherits ENV and WORKDIR"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Inherit vs copy",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Carries over",
            "FROM stage",
            "COPY --from"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Files",
              "yes",
              "chosen paths"
            ],
            [
              "ENV",
              "yes",
              "**no**"
            ],
            [
              "WORKDIR, USER",
              "yes",
              "**no**"
            ],
            [
              "Installed packages",
              "yes",
              "**no**"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "External images",
          "text": "`COPY --from=nginx:1.27` pulls one file from any image, no stage needed."
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Use `FROM stage` to inherit the environment",
            "Use `COPY --from` to ship only chosen files",
            "Name the shared stage `base` for clarity"
          ],
          "style": "checkbox",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Ownership",
          "text": "`COPY --from --chown=app:app /app /app` sets the owner during the copy, with no extra `RUN chown` layer."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "docker",
      "subtitle": "Naming stages"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Build Cache and Layer Ordering",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. What is the cache?",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Every `RUN`, `COPY` and `ADD` makes a ==layer==",
            "Unchanged layers are reused from cache",
            "Key = instruction text + file checksum (COPY/ADD)",
            "One layer invalidated → **all later** layers rebuild"
          ],
          "style": "star",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Order: stable first",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "dockerfile",
          "lines": [
            "COPY package.json package-lock.json ./",
            "# cached until the lockfile changes",
            "RUN npm ci",
            "# changes often, so it comes late",
            "COPY . .",
            "RUN npm run build"
          ],
          "note": "least → most frequently changing"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Go twin",
          "text": "COPY go.mod go.sum ./ → RUN go mod download → COPY . . → RUN go build"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Change",
            "Rebuilt from"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "package-lock.json",
              "npm ci onward"
            ],
            [
              "src/app.js",
              "COPY . . onward"
            ],
            [
              "Base image tag",
              "everything"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Dry run: one edit",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Step",
            "Instruction",
            "Cache"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "1",
              "FROM node:20-alpine",
              "HIT"
            ],
            [
              "2",
              "COPY package*.json ./",
              "HIT"
            ],
            [
              "3",
              "RUN npm ci",
              "HIT"
            ],
            [
              "4",
              "COPY . .",
              "MISS (src edited)"
            ],
            [
              "5",
              "RUN npm run build",
              "MISS (follows)"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 3
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "array",
          "spec": {
            "cells": [
              "FROM",
              "COPY pkg",
              "npm ci",
              "COPY .",
              "build"
            ],
            "indices": true,
            "pointers": [
              {
                "index": 3,
                "label": "edit",
                "ink": "red"
              },
              {
                "index": 4,
                "label": "rebuilt",
                "ink": "red"
              }
            ],
            "highlight": [
              3,
              4
            ],
            "dim": [
              0,
              1,
              2
            ],
            "caption": "cached | invalidated from the edit down"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Stages cache independently: edit runtime, builder stays cached",
            "BuildKit builds independent stages ==in parallel==",
            "Stages not needed by the target are skipped"
          ],
          "style": "dot"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "dockerfile",
          "lines": [
            "RUN apt-get update \\",
            "  && apt-get install -y curl \\",
            "  && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*"
          ],
          "note": "clean in the SAME layer"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`COPY . .` before `npm ci`: any edit reinstalls all deps",
            "`RUN apt-get update` alone gets cached → **stale** lists",
            "`rm` in a later layer: data stays in the earlier layer",
            "Splitting install and cleanup into separate RUN lines"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Force a clean build",
          "text": "`docker build --no-cache --pull .` rebuilds every layer and refreshes base images."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "docker",
      "subtitle": "Layers, keys, order"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "BuildKit Cache Mounts",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. What is it?",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "==BuildKit== is the default builder in modern Docker",
            "Turn on the syntax with `# syntax=docker/dockerfile:1` on line 1",
            "A ==cache mount== is a directory that outlives the build step",
            "It persists on the **builder host**, so a changed lockfile downloads only new packages"
          ],
          "style": "star",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Mechanism: RUN --mount",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "dockerfile",
          "lines": [
            "# syntax=docker/dockerfile:1",
            "FROM node:22 AS build",
            "COPY package*.json ./",
            "RUN --mount=type=cache,\\",
            "  target=/root/.npm npm ci"
          ],
          "note": "cache stays out of the image layer"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Option",
            "What it does"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`id=`",
              "names a cache"
            ],
            [
              "`sharing=`",
              "shared | private | locked"
            ],
            [
              "`mode=` `uid=`",
              "set mount permissions"
            ],
            [
              "`target=`",
              "path inside the build"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Examples: Go, pip, apt",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "dockerfile",
          "lines": [
            "RUN --mount=type=cache,target=/go/pkg/mod \\",
            "  --mount=type=cache,target=/root/.cache/go-build \\",
            "  go build ./...",
            "RUN --mount=type=cache,target=/root/.cache/pip \\",
            "  pip install -r requirements.txt"
          ],
          "note": "one RUN can hold many mounts"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "dockerfile",
          "lines": [
            "RUN --mount=type=cache,target=/var/cache/apt,sharing=locked \\",
            "  --mount=type=cache,target=/var/lib/apt,sharing=locked \\",
            "  apt-get update && apt-get install -y gcc"
          ],
          "note": "apt needs sharing=locked"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Cache mount vs layer cache",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Aspect",
            "Layer cache",
            "Cache mount"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Granularity",
              "whole instruction",
              "inside a RUN"
            ],
            [
              "File changed",
              "rerun, redownload all",
              "**only new** packages"
            ],
            [
              "Lives in",
              "image layers",
              "builder host"
            ],
            [
              "Ships in image",
              "yes",
              "no"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Both stages reuse the same downloaded tarballs",
            "A second stage pays for **no** extra download",
            "Different `id=` values keep caches fully apart"
          ],
          "style": "checkbox",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        }
      ],
      "hero": "docker",
      "subtitle": "mount, cache, secret"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Cache Mount Tuning and Pitfalls",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "CI tip",
          "text": "`--cache-from type=gha --cache-to type=gha` shares **layer** cache between runners; `--mount=type=cache` contents stay on each builder."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Tuning a cache mount",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Name each cache with `id=` to keep projects apart",
            "Same `id=` in two stages shares one cache",
            "`sharing=locked` makes parallel builds take turns",
            "`docker builder prune` clears mount caches too"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "dockerfile",
          "lines": [
            "RUN --mount=type=cache,\\",
            "  id=npm,target=/root/.npm \\",
            "  npm ci"
          ],
          "note": "id names one shared cache"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Share one cache",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "dockerfile",
          "lines": [
            "FROM node:22 AS deps",
            "RUN --mount=type=cache,\\",
            "  id=npm,target=/root/.npm \\",
            "  npm ci --prefer-offline",
            "FROM node:22 AS test",
            "RUN --mount=type=cache,\\",
            "  id=npm,target=/root/.npm \\",
            "  npm ci --prefer-offline"
          ],
          "note": "same id, one cache for both stages"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Pick a sharing mode",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "sharing=",
            "Behaviour",
            "Use for"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`shared`",
              "parallel writers (default)",
              "npm, go, pip"
            ],
            [
              "`private`",
              "fresh copy per build",
              "scratch dirs"
            ],
            [
              "`locked`",
              "one build at a time",
              "apt, dpkg"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "apt cache vanishes?",
          "text": "Debian images ship a `docker-clean` hook that empties apt caches. `rm /etc/apt/apt.conf.d/docker-clean` first to keep the mount useful."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Cache dirs by tool",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Tool",
            "Cache target"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "npm",
              "`/root/.npm`"
            ],
            [
              "pip",
              "`/root/.cache/pip`"
            ],
            [
              "go",
              "`/go/pkg/mod`"
            ],
            [
              "cargo",
              "`/usr/local/cargo/registry`"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "dockerfile",
          "lines": [
            "RUN --mount=type=cache,\\",
            "  target=/usr/local/cargo/registry \\",
            "  cargo build --release"
          ],
          "note": "point target at the tool's cache"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Common mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Wrong `target=` path: the tool never touches the cache",
            "Caching `node_modules` itself: it is **not** in the image",
            "Expecting the cache on a fresh CI runner: it starts empty",
            "Running apt without `sharing=locked` in parallel builds"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Key rule",
          "text": "Layer cache is all-or-nothing per instruction; a cache mount is incremental inside the RUN and never ships."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "docker",
      "subtitle": "mount, cache, secret"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Secret Mounts and Leak Pitfalls",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "dockerfile",
          "lines": [
            "RUN --mount=type=secret,id=npmrc,target=/root/.npmrc \\",
            "  npm ci",
            "# pass it at build time:",
            "# docker build --secret id=npmrc,src=$HOME/.npmrc ."
          ],
          "note": "secret never lands in a layer"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Bind mounts and secrets",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "dockerfile",
          "lines": [
            "RUN --mount=type=bind,source=package.json,target=package.json \\",
            "  npm ls --depth=0"
          ],
          "note": "no COPY layer is created"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Mistakes and limits",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Tokens in `ARG` or `ENV`: **visible** in `docker history` and image metadata",
            "Using `COPY .npmrc` bakes the credential into a layer",
            "Cache mounts are __not shared__ across CI runners by default",
            "`--cache-to` exports **layers** only, never mount contents: keep a persistent builder to reuse them"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Where secrets can leak",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Method",
            "Leaks in image?"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`ARG TOKEN`",
              "yes, `docker history`"
            ],
            [
              "`ENV TOKEN`",
              "yes, metadata"
            ],
            [
              "`COPY .npmrc`",
              "yes, a layer"
            ],
            [
              "`--mount=type=secret`",
              "**no**"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 3,
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "docker build \\",
            "  --cache-to type=registry,ref=r/app \\",
            "  --cache-from type=registry,ref=r/app ."
          ],
          "note": "share cache across CI runners"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Rule of thumb",
          "text": "Cache mounts speed builds up; secret mounts keep credentials out of every layer."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Secret mount details",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Piece",
            "Role"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`id=npmrc`",
              "name matched by --secret"
            ],
            [
              "`target=`",
              "file path during the RUN"
            ],
            [
              "`--secret src=`",
              "host file to read"
            ],
            [
              "after the RUN",
              "mount is gone"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Secret exists only for that one `RUN` instruction",
            "Later `RUN` lines and the final image never see it",
            "Use a ==secret mount== instead of `ARG` for tokens",
            "Pin the id so each credential has its own name"
          ],
          "style": "checkbox",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "docker history --no-trunc app:1.0",
            "# search the output for your token"
          ],
          "note": "audit: a clean build shows nothing"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Audit habit",
          "text": "Run `docker history --no-trunc` on every release image and look for credentials."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "docker",
      "subtitle": "mount, cache, secret"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Final Images: Alpine vs Distroless",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. What Ships",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The ==final stage== decides what ships: pick the **smallest** base that still runs your binary. Everything else stays in the builder.",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`scratch`: empty image, ~0 MB, for fully static binaries",
            "Go needs `CGO_ENABLED=0` to run on scratch",
            "`alpine`: ~5–8 MB, musl libc, busybox, shell and `apk`",
            "`distroless`: no shell, no package manager, only runtime + CA certs",
            "`debian-slim`: ~30–75 MB, glibc, widest compatibility, easy debugging"
          ],
          "style": "star",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Size Comparison",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Go service base",
            "Size"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "golang:1.22",
              "~800 MB"
            ],
            [
              "debian-slim",
              "~85 MB"
            ],
            [
              "alpine",
              "~15 MB"
            ],
            [
              "distroless/static",
              "~8 MB"
            ],
            [
              "scratch",
              "~6 MB"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 4,
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Base",
            "libc",
            "Shell?"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "scratch",
              "none",
              "no"
            ],
            [
              "alpine",
              "musl",
              "yes (ash)"
            ],
            [
              "distroless",
              "glibc/none",
              "no"
            ],
            [
              "debian-slim",
              "glibc",
              "yes (bash)"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Security win",
          "text": "Fewer packages means fewer CVEs in Trivy or Grype and a smaller attack surface."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Scratch Example",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "dockerfile",
          "lines": [
            "FROM golang:1.22 AS build",
            "RUN CGO_ENABLED=0 go build -o /app",
            "FROM scratch",
            "COPY --from=build /etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificates.crt /etc/ssl/certs/",
            "COPY --from=build /app /app"
          ],
          "note": "scratch has no CA certs for HTTPS"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "scratch lacks CA certs, `/etc/passwd`, timezone data",
            "Copy all three from the ==builder stage==",
            "The `COPY --from` line above enables HTTPS calls"
          ],
          "style": "check",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Debug distroless",
          "text": "`docker exec -it c sh` fails. Use the `:debug` tag, `docker debug`, or ephemeral containers."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "**alpine** for a glibc binary built elsewhere: fails with 'not found' at exec",
            "Alpine musl: some Python wheels, Node native addons fail or compile from source",
            "Expecting a shell in distroless, then `exec sh` fails",
            "Forgetting CA certs on scratch: HTTPS calls fail with x509 errors"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        }
      ],
      "hero": "docker",
      "subtitle": "Pick the base"
    },
